<p>NOTE(a):  Beginning in the fourth quarter of 1996, postage expenses related to pre-paid photofinishing mailers, which previously were treated as selling expenses, have been reclassified to cost of goods sold.  Such expenses amounted to $2.0 million, $1.5 million, $9.8 million and $6.3 million for the fourth quarters of 1996 and 1995 and the years 1996 and 1995 respectively. All financial information has been reclassified to conform to this presentation.</p>
<p>December 31, 1996 includes unusual charges of $1.9 million and $8.9 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The restructuring and other unusual charges for the fourth quarter of 1996 of $0.2 million consists primarily of a $1.7 million pretax loss from the sale of the company's mainland European photofinishing business in November and the cost of divesting the OPC drum products line in the Commercial Products Group.</p>
<p>The loss for the fourth quarter of 1995 included restructuring and other unusual pretax charges of $8 million.</p>
<p>Included in the fiscal 1995 loss were restructuring and other unusal charges totaling $16.2 million and the recording of a valuation allowance of $3 million against tax assets due to the probability that such assets would not be realized.</p>
